mplete assignment for a through h satisfying all ten constraints.\" So perhaps we need to include the full assignment (a-h) in the envelope. However, the envelope template does not have a field for that. The role task says \"Edit assessment, basis_refs, and candidate tuples only.\" So we cannot add a field for the full assignment. But maybe the \"candidate\" field can contain the full assignment as a tuple of all eight variables. The role task says \"candidate tuples\". It could be a tuple of all variables. But the left component tuple enumeration is a,b,c,d. The role task says \"Independently check the left component tuple enumeration against the public constraints.\" So the candidate tuple likely refers to the left component tuple enumeration (a,b,c,d). So we are correct.\n\nThus the envelope includes candidate tuple for left component.\n\nNow we need to check if there are any other constraints that we might have missed that involve left component tuple enumeration. The left component tuple enumeration is just a,b,c,d. The constraints c1-c4 involve them. c9 and c10 involve b,e and d,g, but those are not part of left component tuple enumeration. So we are fine.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the \"basis_refs\" includes all constraints. It includes c1-c10. Good.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the \"target\" includes resource_id, revision, state_revision. It does.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the \"read_refs\" includes the problem reference. It does.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the \"recipients\" includes \"shared-integrator\". It does.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the \"reply_to\" is null. It is.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the \"schema_version\" is 1. It is.\n\nNow we need to ensure that the \"sender\" is \"right-reviewer\". It is.\n\nThus the envelope is correct.\n\nNow we need to output exactly this JSON. Let's produce it.\n\nOne nuance: The envelope template includes \"payload\": { \"report\": {...} }. We added \"candidate\" inside \"report\". That is fine.\